  <prompt>Make a provisioned customer BFF start, accept calls from its own Dataverse code pages, and be reachable by the shared M365 clients.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer (L2 control plane, Microsoft Graph application objects, settings catalog).</role>

  <goal>
    After a provisioning run: the customer's BFF starts (its `Cors:AllowedOrigins` is set); its own Dataverse code pages
    sign in through the customer's BFF app registration (H7's default `sprk_MsalClientId`); and the shared add-in client
    can request that BFF's scope without a consent prompt. Re-runs are idempotent.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      `notes/t240-plan.md` F1–F3: CorsModule throws at startup outside Development/Testing when `Cors:AllowedOrigins` is
      empty and no provisioning step sets it; H3 registers no SPA redirect and no preAuthorizedApplications; code pages
      use the Dataverse org origin as their redirect. The add-in client is `c1258e2d…` "Spaarke Office Add-in"
      (single-tenant, Spaarke's tenant). Dev's BFF lists the Dataverse, Power Pages, add-in and Teams origins by hand.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/CorsModule.cs (contract only — not changed)</file>
      <file>scripts/canonical-secret-catalog/manifest.yaml (per_env_settings); the H4b catalog reader + its value-source resolution; HandlerRunInputs (run-context contract)</file>
      <file>src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/EntraAppReg/{GraphAppRegistrationProvisioner,EntraAppRegOptions,H3EntraAppRegHandler}.cs</file>
      <file>src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/E2EAcceptance/E2EValidationRunner.cs (H13 CORS probe)</file>
      <file>docs/guides/SPAARKE-CUSTOMER-DEPLOYMENT-GUIDE.md (H3 row claims add-in SPA redirects); .claude/constraints/provisioning.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/t240-plan.md</file>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/g14-shared-clients-auth-chain.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/provisioning.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-028-spaarke-auth-architecture.md</file>
