    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="cors">Origins are exact (scheme + host, no path, no trailing slash, https only). The customer's Dataverse origin and its `.api.` variant come from the run (H5's DataverseEnvUrl); the shared client origins are platform values (per platform environment), never per-customer intake.</constraint>
    <constraint source="isolation">H3 changes only the customer's own BFF app registration. It never edits a shared Spaarke app (the add-in client, SDAP-PCF-CLIENT).</constraint>
    <constraint source="live">No live Entra or App Service change in this task; tests run against hand-written fakes (never Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;).</constraint>
    <constraint source="scope">The Teams client app does not exist yet: its pre-authorization is wired as configuration that is empty until 240c.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">CORS: catalog entries for `Cors__AllowedOrigins__N` (customer Dataverse origin + `.api.` variant, normalized; shared client origins from a platform option), resolved by H4b; run-context contract kept; tests.</step>
    <step order="2">H3: `spa.redirectUris` = the customer's Dataverse origin(s) (idempotent merge); `api.preAuthorizedApplications` for the configured shared client app ids on the `user_impersonation` scope (idempotent); tests.</step>
    <step order="3">H13: the CORS probe still passes for the Dataverse origin; add a probe for one shared client origin if configured.</step>
    <step order="4">Docs: guide H3/H4b rows, inventory, provisioning.md; the skill's settings list. Verify (ControlPlane, ArchTests, Worker/Api 0 warnings); Step 9.5; close.</step>
  </steps>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">A run's H4b settings include `Cors__AllowedOrigins__0..N`: the customer's Dataverse origin (no trailing slash), its `.api.` variant, and every configured shared client origin; none for an unconfigured origin.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">H3 PATCHes the customer's app registration with those SPA redirect URIs and pre-authorizes each configured client app id on `user_impersonation`; a second run sends no change; it never PATCHes another application.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">An invalid or non-https origin is refused by the run before H4b writes it (named failure).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">ControlPlane tests and ArchTests pass; Worker/Api build with 0 warnings.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>The production add-in / Teams origins are not known yet — ask the owner rather than guess (dev values are known).</trigger>
    <trigger>Graph refuses preAuthorizedApplications for a client in this shape — stop and report.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <notes/>
</task>
